\frac{\partial }{\partial x}\amp \frac{\partial }{\partial y}\amp \frac{\partial }{\partial z}\\
e^{2 y} \amp  \sin^{7} x\amp  \cos^{9} x\end{array}\right|=</me><me>0 \mathbf{i} -\left(-\left(9\cos^{8}\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\sin\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\right)\right) \mathbf{j} +\left(7\sin^{6}\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\cos\mathopen{}\left(x\right)-2e^{2y}\right) \mathbf{k}=</me><me>\left\lt  0, 9\cos^{8}\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\sin\mathopen{}\left(x\right), 7\sin^{6}\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\cos\mathopen{}\left(x\right)-2e^{2y}\right&gt;</me>


